              ],
              "content": "Fig. 5.14: Linear motion"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_13_image_1.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.088,
            0.899,
            0.115,
            0.915
          ],
          "content": "92"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.084,
            0.883,
            0.146
          ],
          "content": "When an object moves along a straight line, its motion is called **linear motion**. **Identify** such linear motion in your surroundings."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.559,
            0.883,
            0.623
          ],
          "content": "But do things always move along a straight line? You might have enjoyed playing on swings and merry-go-rounds. Are these types of motion also linear motion?"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.637,
            0.586,
            0.659
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Activity 5.4: Let us investigate"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.67,
            0.821,
            0.691
          ],
          "content": " Tie an eraser (or a potato) to one end of a thread."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.695,
            0.883,
            0.737
          ],
          "content": " Hold the other end of the thread with your hand and whirl it (Fig. 5.15)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.743,
            0.509,
            0.763
          ],
          "content": "Observe its motion."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.768,
            0.251,
            0.81
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_13_image_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.768,
            0.882,
            0.809
          ],
          "content": "Is the motion of the eraser the same as that of a merry-goround?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.815,
            0.883,
            0.857
          ],
          "content": "When an object moves along a circular path, its motion is called **circular motion.**"
        },
        {
